.SH DESCRIPTION
.B \%winchstr
extracts a
.I curses
character string from a
.I curses
window
.IR win ","
starting at the cursor and stopping at the end of the line,
and stores it in
.IR chstr ","
terminating it with a null
.I curses
character.
.B \%winchnstr
does the same,
but copies at most
.I n
.I curses
characters from
.IR win "."
A negative
.I n
implies no limit;
.B \%winchnstr
then works like
.BR \%winchstr "."
\fB\%ncurses\fP(3X) describes the variants of these functions.
